// doc: Python's built-in round(x) with a single argument rounds a float to
//      the nearest integer, using "round half to even" (banker's rounding):
//      when x is exactly halfway between two integers, the result is the
//      nearest even integer. For example, round(0.5) == 0, round(1.5) == 2,
