// synth: library theory (phase 0)
// doc: Python integer floor division `a // b` for positive `b` truncates toward
// negative infinity. For non-negative `a` and positive `b` this coincides with
// truncation toward zero. In particular, for any integer `n >= 0`,
// `n // 2` equals `n / 2` rounded down (i.e., `(n - (n % 2)) / 2`).
